				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Barry window title\nOwner: CatalystDevKit, BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core (GT/Pharo UI only). Related contract: [[Catalyst framework ownership]], [[Catalyst working rules]], [[Catalyst Fairy]].\n\nCatalyst's world spawn handler gives BVCFairyChat windows the stable title `Barry`, both before and after messages. Ordinary GT chats delegate unchanged to the inherited handler. The only production selector added is {{gtMethod:BVCDevKitWorldElement>>#onGtPhlowObjectToSpawn:}}, an extension owned by BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core. Existing chat tools, composite tabs and pager construction are reused; no replacement dispatcher or chat tool was added."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.069382+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.069382+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "emTwBAdYRBCYZRchO7eGeg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Inspected path and scope\nThe Add chat button creates a registered chat and fires a GtPhlowObjectToSpawn carrying its default inspector tool. GtLChat>>gtDefaultInspectorTool already names the composite; BVCFairyChat>>gtDisplayOn: already includes Barry. Neither is the missing window title source. GtWorldElement>>onGtPhlowObjectToSpawn: creates a BlSpace with inPager: but supplies no title; BlSpace's default title is empty. The Catalyst subclass now sets the title before using that same pager/showFrom: path. GtWorldTabElement>>createBaseTab: copies BlSpace>>title into the tab label. Opening the resulting space natively propagates the title to the host window.\n\nThe separate GtLWorldRegistrySubscriptionHandler path already sets a display-based title and is unchanged. GtLWorldChatRegistryDropdown>>initialize still forwards the spawn without consuming the original. The upstream duplicate-window issue is intentionally untouched. A BVCFairyChat-only display or tool-name override would not repair the world handler's missing title assignment."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.078309+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-21T00:01:33.738232+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "yWuKEzR9RLiVlsq/tSbCPg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Current-image checks\nExecuted in SuperGame.image, Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT, native BlWinitHost. Final BVCFairyWindowTitleExamples run: 4 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skips. Checks cover a newly registered Catalyst chat through world phlow spawn, BlSpace title and tab-label propagation, retained and reopened titles after an offline message, unchanged ordinary GT chat behavior, and the real native host-space title before/after a message. The native example closes its window and checks closure with a 5-second bound. Temporary world tabs and mocked scripter scene children are removed in ensure: blocks; no live provider calls.\n\nExisting popupCreatesCatalystChat also passed (1); GtPhlowChatToolExamples passed all 6 examples with no failures/errors/skips. These are focused checks, not a full DevKit suite. Initial example-authoring runs exposed incorrect test selectors and an incorrect assumption that BlScripterSpace could report closed; corrected before the final green run. BlScripterSpace uses a mocked host and reports open whenever its host exists, so cleanup asserts an empty scene and no host space instead.\n\nExcluded: end-to-end duplicate dropdown-window counts, native title-bar pixels/OS chrome, other platforms, fresh BVC build, source-file save, commit and push. Source changes remain in the image.\n\n## Bounded UI dispatch and recovery repair\nThe preserved helper evaluateOnUIProcess: sent work to the retired BlUniverse default, whose pulse loop was stopped in this image. The active Winit UI uses BlParallelUniverse winit. The helper now reuses that universe through BVCFairyUIRequest, runs directly when already on its UI process, and otherwise waits at most 2000 milliseconds. No second dispatcher is introduced. The request serializes queued/running/finished/abandoned transitions. An abandoned callback cannot execute its body later; parent cancellation and delegation timeout abandon queued requests and wake waiters. A callback already running remains indexed by its owning chat until its ensure: finishes, and keeps the Maintainer gate closed even if the provider reports idle. Request errors preserve their original exception; no process termination or replay is provided.\n\nCurrent-image repair verification: 80 examples passed, zero failures/errors/skips (Fairy 39, continuity 14, Codex 8, presentation 4, titles 4, recovery 11). The recovery checks cover owner-qualified parent/child lookup, reference failures and limits, application-hook avoidance, sensitive fields, bounded process/context metadata, blocked and cross-chat mutation gating, unserviced/late callbacks, cancellation, already-running partial work, original errors and nested direct UI execution. Native Winit title checks passed. The historical stopped test execution 8j0spph1hw6mx1o7sua5z38do was reconciled by identifying and removing each of its four still-queued callbacks through BlUniverse>>undefer:, setting an explicit cancellation error and signaling its wait. No callback body ran during that intervention. The worker then ceased naturally; direct receiver-stack inspection found no live provider frames, its provider became idle, and the retired queue was empty. Its timeout and cancellation evidence remain retained. Cessation does not imply that its interrupted checks succeeded.\n\nLive Codex acceptance: Barry called inspectLiveObject directly; one default-tool Explorer inspected the same retained execution, a primitive array in its child's owning storage (42), and the historical execution. Inspection worked while the controlled Maintainer remained stopping and the mutation gate remained closed. The controlled fixture was cleared afterward. Existing Barry chats received the tool through refreshInstructions without replacing their providers, clients or histories. Partial UI source was preserved. Fresh BVC rebuild survival of this repair remains to be checked; native TLS failures, arbitrary application threads and GemStone are outside this GT-only repair."
			},
